.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-staging-clean 1  "tapectl-staging-clean " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-staging\-clean \- Clean staged files from disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl staging clean\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-unit\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clean staged files from disk
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Clean all staged sets, not just those with completed writes; also releases a unit\*(Aqs staged data that a bare `staging clean` would otherwise retain for being below its policy\*(Aqs resolved min_copies (issue #244, #262)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it (issue #241)
.TP
\fB\-\-unit\fR \fI<UNIT>\fR
Narrow which staged sets are considered for release to this unit (repeatable) \-\- issue #274. Without `\-\-force`, the same min_copies split still applies within the named unit(s): one below its own resolved min_copies keeps its staged bytes retained (pass `\-\-force` to release it too, exactly as for the whole\-archive form). A `\*(Aqfailed\*(Aq` stage_set is always swept regardless of this scope \-\- see `CleanScope::Units`\*(Aqs own contract in `src/staging/clean.rs`. An unknown unit name is an error, not a silent no\-op
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept (issue #147)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
